{"kind": "result", "at": "2026-11-02T18:33:50.533720+00:00", "task": "app_migration", "attempt": 2, "trial_id": "t-f693b12d3f13465ba18574f81ea4aa78", "verdict": "INFRA_ERROR", "reason": "behavioral_job:eso_not_synced", "s": 607.4, "view": {"trial_id": "t-f693b12d3f13465ba18574f81ea4aa78", "plan_id": "778b074a-a07a-4362-8987-0481e4aa4e67", "rehearsal_id": "bcea2d5b-c1f2-410b-acd7-f9c9f10fbdad", "attempt": 2, "task": "app-migration", "role": "app_migration", "phase": "done", "verdict": "INFRA_ERROR", "reason": "behavioral_job:eso_not_synced", "artifact": {"plan_id": "p-778b074a-a07a-4362-8987-0481e4aa4e67", "trial_id": "t-f693b12d3f13465ba18574f81ea4aa78", "attempt": 2, "rationale": "Removed the direct Secrets Manager SDK path (boto3.client('secretsmanager') at secrets.py:41 and get_secret_value at secrets.py:48; evidence inv:3ccbf876f57f08e8, inv:9de663601b600ca9) and its selection branch. The DB password is now read only from the file at DB_PASSWORD_FILE (destination mounts ESO-synced Secret bravo-demo-db at /var/run/bravo/db/password). config.load() no longer requires DB_PASSWORD_SOURCE / DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_ID / DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_KEY / DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_REGION / AWS_REGION / DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_ENDPOINT_URL; it requires DB_DSN (unchanged, inv:a5ccbeca75df0ace) and DB_PASSWORD_FILE. DbSettings keeps password_source (constant 'env-file') so the existing startup log in app.py stays unchanged; secret_id/secret_key/secrets_region/secrets_endpoint_url fields were dropped (only secrets.py used them; checked app.py, db.py, admin.py, telemetry.py, __main__.py). DSN/attachments/S3 config (inv:baa6de5a5e72c850, inv:4b2a570efa066af8 left as-is: already endpoint-from-config), write-block switch and logging are untouched. No dependencies, tests, CI or deployment files changed. Note: one line in config.py (DSN password guard) is shown as '[redacted]' by the tool layer; it was rebuilt verbatim (make_diff showed no change there in an intermediate run) and the final diff deliberately has no hunk touching that line, so -p1 application isn't affected by the redaction. The original error message on that line still mentions DB_PASSWORD_SOURCE (cosmetic only). compile passed; the diff is the make_diff output with no edits. Risk medium: the search check was not usable (rg missing), so field usage was checked by reading the files by hand; tests that reference the removed fields (if any) were not run.", "risk": "medium", "evidence_refs": ["inv:3ccbf876f57f08e8", "inv:9de663601b600ca9", "inv:a5ccbeca75df0ace", "inv:baa6de5a5e72c850", "inv:4b2a570efa066af8"], "role": "app_migration", "step": "fix", "diff": "diff -ruN src/src/bravo_demo/config.py app/src/bravo_demo/config.py\n--- src/src/bravo_demo/config.py\t1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000\n+++ app/src/bravo_demo/config.py\t2026-11-02 18:28:55.525835458 +0000\n@@ -70,12 +70,8 @@\n class DbSettings:\n     # libpq DSN without the password, e.g. \"host=pgbouncer port=6432 dbname=chat user=app_writer\".\n     dsn: str\n-    password_source: str  # aws-secrets-manager | env-file\n-    password_file: str | None\n-    secret_id: str | None\n-    secret_key: str | None  # JSON key inside the secret; None = the secret string is the password\n-    secrets_region: str | None\n-    secrets_endpoint_url: str | None\n+    password_source: str  # always env-file: the password comes from the mounted DB_PASSWORD_FILE\n+    password_file: str\n     pool_min: int\n     pool_max: int\n     statement_timeout_ms: int  # per write transaction (SET LOCAL), §8.10 max 200 ms\n@@ -147,18 +143,11 @@\n     keys, an on-prem S3-compatible store): there is no per-cloud code path.\"\"\"\n     env = dict(os.environ) if env is None else env\n \n-    source = _req(env, \"DB_PASSWORD_SOURCE\")\n-    if source not in (\"aws-secrets-manager\", \"env-file\"):\n-        raise ConfigError(\"DB_PASSWORD_SOURCE must be aws-secrets-manager or env-file\")\n     statement_timeout_ms = _int(env, \"DB_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS\", 200, 10, 200)\n     db = DbSettings(\n         dsn=_req(env, \"DB_DSN\"),\n-        password_source=source,\n-        password_file=_req(env, \"DB_PASSWORD_FILE\") if source == \"env-file\" else None,\n-        secret_id=_req(env, \"DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_ID\") if source == \"aws-secrets-manager\" else None,\n-        secret_key=_opt(env, \"DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_KEY\"),\n-        secrets_region=_opt(env, \"DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_REGION\") or _opt(env, \"AWS_REGION\"),\n-        secrets_endpoint_url=_opt(env, \"DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_ENDPOINT_URL\"),\n+        password_source=\"env-file\",  # noqa: S106 - a mode name, not a secret\n+        password_file=_req(env, \"DB_PASSWORD_FILE\"),\n         pool_min=_int(env, \"DB_POOL_MIN\", 1, 0, 50),\n         pool_max=_int(env, \"DB_POOL_MAX\", 8, 1, 100),\n         statement_timeout_ms=statement_timeout_ms,\ndiff -ruN src/src/bravo_demo/secrets.py app/src/bravo_demo/secrets.py\n--- src/src/bravo_demo/secrets.py\t1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000\n+++ app/src/bravo_demo/secrets.py\t2026-11-02 18:28:16.724060819 +0000\n@@ -1,14 +1,12 @@\n-\"\"\"Database password sources (§8.10).\n+\"\"\"Database password source (§8.10).\n \n-``aws-secrets-manager`` calls the AWS Secrets Manager API directly with the SDK at startup.\n-This direct cloud dependency is intentional: it is the \"code fix\" material of scenario S2.\n-``env-file`` reads a mounted file (Kubernetes Secret, Docker secret); this is the mode the\n-fix switches to, so the app no longer calls a cloud API.\n+The password is read only from a mounted file (``DB_PASSWORD_FILE``): on the landing zone ESO\n+syncs it from the platform OpenBao into a Kubernetes Secret that is mounted into the pod. The app\n+calls no cloud API and needs no cloud credentials.\n \"\"\"\n \n from __future__ import annotations\n \n-import json\n import logging\n from pathlib import Path\n \n@@ -31,51 +29,9 @@\n     return value\n \n \n-def _from_secrets_manager(settings: DbSettings) -> str:\n-    import boto3  # imported here: the env-file mode must not need AWS at all\n-    from botocore.config import Config\n-    from botocore.exceptions import BotoCoreError, ClientError\n-\n-    if not settings.secret_id:\n-        raise ConfigError(\"DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_ID is required\")\n-    client = boto3.client(\n-        \"secretsmanager\",\n-        region_name=settings.secrets_region,\n-        endpoint_url=settings.secrets_endpoint_url,\n-        config=Config(connect_timeout=3, read_timeout=5, retries={\"max_attempts\": 3, \"mode\": \"standard\"}),\n-    )\n-    try:\n-        resp = client.get_secret_value(SecretId=settings.secret_id)\n-    except ClientError as exc:\n-        code = exc.response.get(\"Error\", {}).get(\"Code\", \"Unknown\")\n-        raise SecretError(f\"Secrets Manager GetSecretValue failed: {code}\") from exc\n-    except BotoCoreError as exc:\n-        raise SecretError(f\"Secrets Manager call failed: {type(exc).__name__}\") from exc\n-    raw = resp.get(\"SecretString\")\n-    if raw is None:\n-        raise SecretError(\"secret has no SecretString\")\n-    if settings.secret_key:\n-        try:\n-            doc = json.loads(raw)\n-        except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n-            raise SecretError(\"secret is not JSON but DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_KEY is set\") from exc\n-        value = doc.get(settings.secret_key) if isinstance(doc, dict) else None\n-        if not isinstance(value, str) or not value:\n-            raise SecretError(\"secret JSON has no string value for DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_KEY\")\n-        return value\n-    if not raw:\n-        raise SecretError(\"secret string is empty\")\n-    return raw\n-\n-\n def db_password(settings: DbSettings) -> str:\n-    if settings.password_source == \"env-file\":  # noqa: S105 - a mode name, not a secret\n-        if not settings.password_file:\n-            raise ConfigError(\"DB_PASSWORD_FILE is required\")\n-        value = _from_file(settings.password_file)\n-    elif settings.password_source == \"aws-secrets-manager\":  # noqa: S105 - a mode name\n-        value = _from_secrets_manager(settings)\n-    else:  # config.load() rejects anything else\n-        raise ConfigError(\"unknown DB_PASSWORD_SOURCE\")\n+    if not settings.password_file:\n+        raise ConfigError(\"DB_PASSWORD_FILE is required\")\n+    value = _from_file(settings.password_file)\n     log.info(\"database password loaded\", extra={\"source\": settings.password_source})\n     return value\n", "files": ["src/bravo_demo/secrets.py", "src/bravo_demo/config.py"], "sdk_calls_replaced": [{"file": "src/bravo_demo/secrets.py", "line": 41, "before_api": "boto3.client('secretsmanager')", "after": "removed; password read from mounted file DB_PASSWORD_FILE"}, {"file": "src/bravo_demo/secrets.py", "line": 48, "before_api": "secretsmanager.GetSecretValue", "after": "_from_file(settings.password_file) (ESO-synced Kubernetes Secret mount)"}], "config_changes": [{"key": "DB_PASSWORD_SOURCE", "before": "required (aws-secrets-manager | env-file)", "after": "removed; not read"}, {"key": "DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_ID", "before": "required when source=aws-secrets-manager", "after": "removed; not read"}, {"key": "DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_KEY", "before": "optional JSON key inside the secret", "after": "removed; not read"}, {"key": "DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_REGION", "before": "optional, fallback AWS_REGION", "after": "removed; not read"}, {"key": "DB_PASSWORD_SECRET_ENDPOINT_URL", "before": "optional Secrets Manager endpoint", "after": "removed; not read"}, {"key": "DB_PASSWORD_FILE", "before": "required only when source=env-file", "after": "always required (/var/run/bravo/db/password on target-onprem)"}]}, "artifact_digest": "sha256:9df7ba81c9f5d45f0472d6be21c52051c36bcf9c6e67333ba183a127b5e6a88e", "verifier": {"run_id": "verify-778b074a-app-2/verify-runner-t-f693b12d3f", "pod_uid": "d4b6eaa9-b1ff-40ed-9c1d-44c1c5770c13", "image_digest": "sha256:6dd8b6dab6b3adc7812bab69eca5dbdc1a5cc690ad28306d234ffb4ef8ac9753", "image_id": "docker.io/library/import-2026-11